    "summary": "Single-span simply supported precast prestressed small-box-girder bridge, 25 m bearing-centre-to-centre, deck width 16 m, carriageway 15 m, one-way traffic, 4 design lanes, Highway Class II (JTG D60-2015).\n\nModel: 2D spine beam, simply_supported system; 5 girders merged into one beam using the middle-girder midspan section (single A=1.0605 m², I=0.2517 m⁴; combined A=5.3026 m², I=1.2583 m⁴), C40 (Ec=32500 MPa, γ=26 kN/m³), girder self-weight only (w=137.87 kN/m, m=14.05 t/m). Both abutments carry 10 plain laminated elastomeric bearings per line (300×350 mm, 4×8 mm rubber layers, S=10.10), modelled as vertical and longitudinal springs (Kv=1.416e7 kN/m, Kh=3.281e4 kN/m), rotation free. Lane load: qk=7.875 kN/m, Pk.1=232.5 kN, 4 lanes ξ=0.67, impact factor μ=0.2409 from f1=4.2716 Hz (JTG D60-2015 4.3.2).\n\nRoot cause of the initial failure: the instance layer had the plain elastomeric bearings flagged as longitudinally fixed (fixed:true), inconsistent with the description and with MR-03, which models plain laminated elastomeric bearings as longitudinal shear springs. Correcting the instance (fixed:false) invalidated the dependent lane decision, which then exposed a second error: lane.qk had been accepted as 10.5 kN/m (Class I value) whereas the Class II formula gives 0.75×10.5=7.875 kN/m. Both were repaired.\n\nResults: f1=4.2716 Hz (within the empirical range for 25 m); self-weight support reactions 1723.35+1723.35=3446.7 kN = γ·A·L; self-weight midspan moment 10770.9 kN·m; lane-load maximum positive moment 6878.4 kN·m. Model now passes L1/L2/L3."
